  "method": "Three worker restarts per build; each restart runs the same 20-case first sweep then warm sweep. Only the first case in each first sweep is isolate-cold; other routes are first visits in that isolate. V8 sampling interval 100us. Sampled active-stack durations exclude idle/program, include GC; these are profiler estimates, not Cloudflare billable CPU or HTTP durations. Classification is exclusive by matching stack ancestors, with formatting/catalog/serialization/runtime config before Vue. Async work outside those stacks can appear in other.",
  "limitations": [
    "V8 active-stack sampling is an estimate and includes profiler/local runtime overhead. It is not Cloudflare billed CPU and is not derived from HTTP elapsed time.",
    "Each first sweep starts a new worker. Only its first case is isolate-cold. The first baseline round also initialized the persisted content database; cold totals are descriptive and cannot cleanly isolate the code change. Warm sweeps are the primary comparison.",
    "Content inputs were unchanged and the AI snapshot was frozen. SQLite file hashes changed when rebuilding, so binary database identity is not asserted. Both builds used the same 25-post dataset and smoke used the database belonging to the final build.",
    "Categories with fewer than 11 posts cannot exercise a real second page: page=2 requests cover the existing clamp behavior there. /posts has a real second page.",
    "Only local results are measured for this patch. CI deployment and post-deployment Cloudflare cpuTime/exceededCpu/Ray ID verification remain pending."
  ],
